{"key":"d75682ac543d22a4","source_file":"Potts Ph - Po.json","source_id":14439,"source_url":"concordance-please-ppl-placere","term":"Please","headwords":["Please","Pleasure","Complacency"],"latin":["Placere","Placitus","Complacentia"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Please"],"latin":["Placere"]},{"english":["Pleasure"],"latin":["Placitus"]},{"english":["Complacency"],"latin":["Complacentia"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AC","AE","AR","SE","TCR"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"1483","subsection":null},"text":"That they were pleasing. Signified. See AC 1480:end.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"5304","subsection":null},"text":"The word was good in the eyes of Pharaoh = the complacency of the Natural. The word good = to please.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"6624","subsection":null},"text":"When the Lord so pleases.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AR","section":"31","subsection":null},"text":"The Lord has pleased to describe...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"341","subsection":null},"text":"From freedom and pleasure... TCR 425.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"SE","section":"4843","subsection":"2"},"text":"Say... whatever pleases another.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"324","subsection":"20"},"text":"Complacency, occurs.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"866","subsection":"8"},"text":"The things which inflow into the thought are like objects... of which some please, and some do not please; and those which please enter the delight of his life, but those which do not please are rejected. Thus is it with everything which inflows into man's internal sight... If it pleases, it enters his will, and adds itself to his life; but if it does not please, it is rejected.","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"please","url":"/meta/potts/please/"}